{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781015351499,"sessionID":"ses_153369dedffemeV7129OxwCDlM","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tooluse_YOIY8lxvUtRupubLEaiUt5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_prompt_20260609.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_prompt_20260609.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Research Gate Tuning Knobs\n2: \n3: You are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n4: \n5: ## Goal\n6: Add opt-in P10 Research Gate tuning knobs so P10 can be tested with relaxed gate policies without changing default strict behavior.\n7: \n8: ## Scope\n9: Allowed files only:\n10: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n11: - `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n12: - `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n13: - `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md`\n14: \n15: Do not modify unrelated files. Do not commit/push.\n16: \n17: ## Context\n18: Strict matrix results: all P10 horizon configs had `Fallbacks=8/8`, `NonEmptyHorizonFolds=0`. Research Gate excludes all horizons, so P10 blend rarely runs.\n19: \n20: Current approved P10 constraints must remain:\n21: - default strict behavior unchanged\n22: - P10 remains default-off\n23: - relaxed gate must be explicit opt-in\n24: - negative/zero final-objective quality gets zero weight\n25: - no abs(IC), no equal-weight fallback\n26: - all invalid/non-positive horizons fallback T+5 baseline\n27: - PIT safe: use train/validation only\n28: \n29: ## Required implementation\n30: \n31: ### 1) Engine params\n32: Add constructor params with defaults preserving current behavior:\n33: - `p10_gate_mode: str = \"strict\"`\n34:   - valid: `strict`, `relaxed`\n35: - `p10_gate_min_pass: int = 1`\n36:   - minimum true gate passes required for a horizon\n37: - `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates: bool = False`\n38:   - strict default false for P10 horizon eligibility\n39:   - relaxed mode may allow candidates selected by top_alphas only if their final-objective selected quality is positive later\n40: \n41: Validate values.\n42: \n43: ### 2) Horizon gate eligibility\n44: In `_compute_horizon_signal()`:\n45: - strict mode: current robust pass count logic unchanged.\n46: - relaxed mode: allow horizon to proceed if either:\n47:   - robust pass count >= `p10_gate_min_pass`, OR\n48:   - `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates=True` and `top_alphas` non-empty.\n49: - Even in relaxed mode, include diagnostics:\n50:   - gate_mode\n51:   - gate_passed_count\n52:   - gate_required_passes\n53:   - used_fallback_candidates bool\n54: - Do not mark failed gate verdicts as passed; just allow candidate continuation when explicitly configured.\n55: - Blend quality guard later must still reject non-positive final-objective IC.\n56: \n57: ### 3) CLI flags\n58: Add to `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`:\n59: - `--p10-gate-mode strict|relaxed`, default `strict`\n60: - `--p10-gate-min-pass`, int default `1`\n61: - `--p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates`, action store_true default false\n62: \n63: Pass to engine. Persist in JSON config.\n64: \n65: ### 4) Tests\n66: Add tests proving:\n67: - default strict behavior unchanged: FAIL string horizon excluded.\n68: - relaxed mode without fallback candidates still excludes all FAIL if min pass unmet.\n69: - relaxed + allow fallback candidates lets horizon compute a signal if candidates exist.\n70: - relaxed admitted horizon with negative/zero final-objective quality still gets zero weight / fallback.\n71: - invalid gate mode raises.\n72: - CLI args parse/persist if there are existing CLI tests; otherwise unit-test engine only.\n73: \n74: ### 5) Verification\n75: Run:\n76: ```powershell\n77: python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\n78: python -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\n79: python scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --quick-mode --multi-horizon-blend --blend-horizons 1,3,5 --p10-gate-mode relaxed --p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates\n80: ```\n81: \n82: ### 6) Report\n83: Write `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md` with:\n84: - files changed\n85: - knobs added\n86: - defaults unchanged proof\n87: - tests/results\n88: - residual risks\n89: \n90: Do not commit/push.\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Research Gate Tuning Knobs\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Goal\nAdd opt-in P10 Research Gate tuning knobs so P10 can be tested with relaxed gate policies without changing default strict behavior.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md`\n\nDo not modify unrelated files. Do not commit/push.\n\n## Context\nStrict matrix results: all P10 horizon configs had `Fallbacks=8/8`, `NonEmptyHorizonFolds=0`. Research Gate excludes all horizons, so P10 blend rarely runs.\n\nCurrent approved P10 constraints must remain:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_prompt_20260609.md","text":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Research Gate Tuning Knobs\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Goal\nAdd opt-in P10 Research Gate tuning knobs so P10 can be tested with relaxed gate policies without changing default strict behavior.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md`\n\nDo not modify unrelated files. Do not commit/push.\n\n## Context\nStrict matrix results: all P10 horizon configs had `Fallbacks=8/8`, `NonEmptyHorizonFolds=0`. Research Gate excludes all horizons, so P10 blend rarely runs.\n\nCurrent approved P10 constraints must remain:\n- default strict behavior unchanged\n- P10 remains default-off\n- relaxed gate must be explicit opt-in\n- negative/zero final-objective quality gets zero weight\n- no abs(IC), no equal-weight fallback\n- all invalid/non-positive horizons fallback T+5 baseline\n- PIT safe: use train/validation only\n\n## Required implementation\n\n### 1) Engine params\nAdd constructor params with defaults preserving current behavior:\n- `p10_gate_mode: str = \"strict\"`\n  - valid: `strict`, `relaxed`\n- `p10_gate_min_pass: int = 1`\n  - minimum true gate passes required for a horizon\n- `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates: bool = False`\n  - strict default false for P10 horizon eligibility\n  - relaxed mode may allow candidates selected by top_alphas only if their final-objective selected quality is positive later\n\nValidate values.\n\n### 2) Horizon gate eligibility\nIn `_compute_horizon_signal()`:\n- strict mode: current robust pass count logic unchanged.\n- relaxed mode: allow horizon to proceed if either:\n  - robust pass count >= `p10_gate_min_pass`, OR\n  - `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates=True` and `top_alphas` non-empty.\n- Even in relaxed mode, include diagnostics:\n  - gate_mode\n  - gate_passed_count\n  - gate_required_passes\n  - used_fallback_candidates bool\n- Do not mark failed gate verdicts as passed; just allow candidate continuation when explicitly configured.\n- Blend quality guard later must still reject non-positive final-objective IC.\n\n### 3) CLI flags\nAdd to `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`:\n- `--p10-gate-mode strict|relaxed`, default `strict`\n- `--p10-gate-min-pass`, int default `1`\n- `--p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates`, action store_true default false\n\nPass to engine. Persist in JSON config.\n\n### 4) Tests\nAdd tests proving:\n- default strict behavior unchanged: FAIL string horizon excluded.\n- relaxed mode without fallback candidates still excludes all FAIL if min pass unmet.\n- relaxed + allow fallback candidates lets horizon compute a signal if candidates exist.\n- relaxed admitted horizon with negative/zero final-objective quality still gets zero weight / fallback.\n- invalid gate mode raises.\n- CLI args parse/persist if there are existing CLI tests; otherwise unit-test engine only.\n\n### 5) Verification\nRun:\n```powershell\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\npython scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --quick-mode --multi-horizon-blend --blend-horizons 1,3,5 --p10-gate-mode relaxed --p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates\n```\n\n### 6) Report\nWrite `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md` with:\n- files changed\n- knobs added\n- defaults unchanged proof\n- tests/results\n- residual risks\n\nDo not commit/push.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":90,"totalLines":90,"truncated":false}},"title":".ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_prompt_20260609.md","time":{"start":1781015351475,"end":1781015351495}},"id":"prt_eacc98c7c001aI4piYjlPhUCL8","sessionID":"ses_153369dedffemeV7129OxwCDlM","messageID":"msg_eacc96367001gVS8DCx971xcbB"}}
