{"type":"text","timestamp":1781015791003,"sessionID":"ses_153369dedffemeV7129OxwCDlM","part":{"id":"prt_eacd014a9001xEyF7PbcTOTyfS","messageID":"msg_eacd00599001vKhaT9E3zMnclY","sessionID":"ses_153369dedffemeV7129OxwCDlM","type":"text","text":"<thinking>\nThe user wants me to continue, but I've actually completed all the tasks specified in the prompt. All 8 tasks are marked as completed. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of what was accomplished.\n\nThe implementation is complete:\n1. All code changes made to the 3 files as specified\n2. All tests written and passing (148 total tests, including 8 new gate tuning tests)\n3. Integration test successful with relaxed gate mode\n4. Comprehensive implementation report written\n\nI should provide a clear summary to the user explaining that the task is complete and ready for the next phase (L3 Audit as mentioned in the prompt).\n</thinking>\n\n## P10 Gate Tuning Implementation - COMPLETE ✓\n\nAll tasks from the prompt have been successfully executed. Here's the final summary:\n\n### Implementation Complete\n\n**Files Modified** (3):\n1. `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py` - Engine with gate tuning logic\n2. `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py` - CLI flags and integration\n3. `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py` - Comprehensive test coverage\n\n### Knobs Added (3)\n\n**Engine Parameters:**\n- `p10_gate_mode: str = \"strict\"` - Gate policy mode\n- `p10_gate_min_pass: int = 1` - Minimum passes required\n- `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates: bool = False` - Fallback allowance\n\n**CLI Flags:**\n- `--p10-gate-mode {strict,relaxed}`\n- `--p10-gate-min-pass INT`\n- `--p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates`\n\n### Verification Results\n\n**Unit Tests:** ✓ 148/148 PASSED\n- 36 existing P10 multi-horizon tests: PASS\n- 8 new gate tuning tests: PASS\n- 104 other phase35 tests: PASS\n\n**Integration Test:** ✓ PASS\n- Backtest with `--p10-gate-mode relaxed --p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates`\n- Relaxed gate correctly used fallback candidates\n- Quality guard correctly triggered baseline fallback for non-positive IC\n- Comprehensive diagnostics logged\n\n### Key Implementation Highlights\n\n1. **Default Behavior Preserved**: All parameters default to strict mode\n2. **Explicit Opt-In**: Relaxed mode requires explicit CLI flags\n3. **Quality Guard Active**: Non-positive final-objective IC still triggers fallback\n4. **PIT Safety Maintained**: All gate decisions use train/validation data only\n5. **Zero Breaking Changes**: 100% backward compatible\n\n### Implementation Report\n\nComplete report written to: `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_report_20260609.md`\n\nContains:\n- Files changed with line counts\n- Knobs added with behavior matrix\n- Defaults unchanged proof\n- Test results and verification commands\n- Residual risk analysis\n- Approved P10 constraints verification\n\n---\n\n**Status**: Ready for L3 Audit (Codex review as specified in AGENTS.md SOD protocol)\n\n**Next Steps** (per prompt requirements):\n- Do not commit/push (as instructed)\n- L3 Audit session should review implementation report\n- If approved, proceed to git operations","time":{"start":1781015778473,"end":1781015791000}}}
